Third-party components
======================

Apache-2.0 applies to Keywright's own code and documentation. Dependencies,
container base images, optional services and embedding models retain their own
licenses. This file is a guide to those components, not a replacement for their
license texts or a complete inventory of a particular image.

Python dependencies
-------------------
Keywright distributions declare dependencies rather than vendoring them. pip
installs their license files alongside their package metadata, typically under
/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/<distribution>.dist-info/ in the supplied
images. Preserve those files when redistributing an installation or image.
The pyproject.toml files declare the dependency ranges; resolved versions may
change between builds.

AsyncSSH is used as an unmodified library under EPL-2.0. Its installed asyncssh/
directory contains the Python source, including upstream copyright headers;
its distribution metadata includes the Eclipse Public License text. Source and
release history: https://github.com/ronf/asyncssh

Certifi uses MPL-2.0 for its certificate bundle. The installed certifi/ directory
contains the bundle and Python source, and its distribution metadata includes
the license. Source and release history: https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi

Container operating-system packages
-----------------------------------
The images use the official Python slim image and Debian packages. License and
copyright notices are retained under /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright and in
Python's installation. Debian source packages are available through the Debian
archive and https://snapshot.debian.org/ for the corresponding package version.
Some system tools have copyleft licenses; redistributors must satisfy their
source-distribution requirements as well as retaining notices. Before publishing
a release image, audit its exact installed versions and provide any required
corresponding-source materials. A Keywright image license label describes the
Keywright application, not every component in the image.

Optional services
-----------------
PostgreSQL, pgvector, LiteLLM and any embedding server/model are separate services
with their own upstream terms. Check the particular image and model version you
deploy or redistribute. Keywright's license does not relicense those services.
